WHAT THIS PROJECT IS
--------------------
A Linux port of `cell-stream-server`, the Windows-side counterpart of the PS3
homebrew application `cell-stream` from ps3-dev (release 174-a5dd795). It
captures the desktop, encodes H.264, streams it to a PlayStation 3 over UDP and
replays the console's controller on the PC.

The PS3 application itself is NOT part of this repository and is NOT modified by
it. This server speaks the same wire protocol so that the unmodified `cell-stream`
package works with it.

THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL INCLUDED HERE
----------------------------------
`upstream/` holds unmodified copies of the original sources, kept for reference
so that this port can be checked against what it was ported from:

  upstream/server/      C# sources of the original Windows server, its README
                        and its build-ffmpeg.sh          (mohasi, Apache-2.0)
  upstream/server/cell-stream.ico
                        the original application icon    (mohasi, Apache-2.0)
  upstream/ps3-app/     the PS3 application's README plus the source files that
                        define the wire protocol (stream.c, stream.h,
                        net-common.c, net-common.h)      (mohasi, Apache-2.0)
  upstream/SOURCE.txt   which upstream commit these copies came from

The application icons under `data/icons/` are derived from the original
`cell-stream.ico` (mohasi, Apache-2.0); the grey/green status dots are original
to this project.

At runtime this project drives, but does not include or link, the following:
FFmpeg, GStreamer, xdg-desktop-portal, PipeWire, GTK4 and libadwaita, all
installed from the distribution's own packages.

WHAT IS ORIGINAL TO THIS PROJECT
--------------------------------
Everything under `src/`, `tests/`, `packaging/` and `data/` other than the
derived icons: the Python implementation, the Linux-specific capture, input,
display and audio paths, the packaging, the test suite and the documentation.
